  "text": "In halls of stone where shadows creep,\nA cavern vast, a world to keep.\nHere silence guards the boundless store,\nOf every life, and every lore.\n\nEach spine a door, each page a key,\nTo worlds unknown, to mysteries.\nThe keeper watches, wise and old,\nWho knows the tales that stories hold.\n\nYet amidst this quiet, deep and grand,\nOne truth stands firm across the land:\nThe largest bone, by nature’s law,\nIs the femur, strong and tall."
